    "content" : "1 Introduction and main results"
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 13,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 123.27, 540.128, 192.992 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "In recent years, models related to KPZ growth in a half-space were extensively studied. For example, [1] studied the ﬂuctuations of last passage percolation with exponential weights in a half-quadrant within the framework of Pfaﬃan Schur processes, [17] shows the ﬂuctuations of a one-dimensional polynuclear growth model in a half-space, the log-gamma polymer in a half space was also considered [13]. For a large amount of half-space models, the ﬂuctuations follow the GUE Tracy Widom distribution in the bulk. It is interesting to further investigate if these models converges to the Airy line ensemble."
  }, {
    "type" : "paragraph",
    "pdfua_tag" : "P",
    "id" : 14,
    "page number" : 1,
    "bounding box" : [ 72.0, 99.39, 540.116, 122.711 ],
    "font" : "CMR10",
    "font size" : 9.963,
    "text color" : "[0.0]",
    "content" : "The Airy line ensemble LAiry is a random sequence of continuous functions that arises as a scaling limit in random matrix theory and various models within the KPZ universality class [5, 6, 15, 18]. In particular,"
